1 NOTE {geni:about_me} #I (am) the lady Adda-guppi’, mother
2 CONT #of Nabium-na’id, king of Babylon,
2 CONT #votaress of the gods Sin, Nin-gal, Nusku, and Sadarnunna, my deities
2 CONT #who, from my childhood, have sought after
2 CONT #their godheads. Whereas in the i6th year of Nabopolassar,
2 CONT #king of Babylon, Sin, king of the gods, with his city
2 CONT #and his temple was angry and went up to heaven-the city and
2 CONT #the people that (were) in it went to ruin.
2 CONT #(Now) forasmuch as the shrines of Sin, Nin-gal, Nusku,
2 CONT #and Sadarnunna I sought after and was worshipper of their godhead,
2 CONT #(and) that I laid hold on the hem of the robe of Sin, king of the gods, night and daytime
2 CONT #I had ever in mind his great godhead@aily, without ceaSing,
2 CONT #of Sin, gamag, Igtar, and Adda, so long as I am alive,
2 CONT #I (am) their votaress (both) in heaven and earth. My blesSings,
2 CONT #the goodly things which they gave me, I (too) by day, night, month, and year, gave (back) to them.
2 CONT #I laid hold on the hem of the robe of Sin, king of the gods, night and daytime
2 CONT #my two eyes were with him, in prayer and humility of face
2 CONT #was I bowed before them (and) thus (I prayed), " May thy return
2 CONT #to thy city be (vouchsafed) to me, that the people, the black-headed,
2 CONT #may worship thy great godhead." For calming
2 CONT #the heart of my god and my goddess, a dress of fine wool, jewels,
2 CONT #silver, gold, a new shift, perfumes, sweet oil,
2 CONT #applied not to my body, (but in) a torn shift
2 CONT #I went clothed, my goings-out were noiseless, I proclaimed
2 CONT #their praises : the glory of my city and of my goddess
2 CONT #was (ever) set in my heart, I kept watch upon them,
2 CONT #anything good of mine I did not omit, but carried it (ever) before them.
2 CONT #From the 2oth year of Assurbanipal, king of Assyria, that I was born (in)
2 CONT #until the 42nd year of Assurbanipal, the 3rd year of Asur-etillu-ili,
2 CONT #his son, the 2 I St year of Nabopolassar, the 43rd year of Nebuchadrezzar,
2 CONT #the 2nd year of Awel-Marduk, the 4th year of Neriglissar,
2 CONT #in 95 years of the god Sin, king of the gods of heaven and earth,
2 CONT #(in) which I sought after the shrines of his great godhead,
2 CONT #(for) my good doings he looked upon me with a smile
2 CONT #he heard my prayers, he granted my saying, the wrath
2 CONT #of his heart calmed. Towards E-hul-hul the temple of Sin
2 CONT #which (is) in Harran, the abode of his heart’s delight, he was reconciled, he had
2 CONT #regard. Sin, king of the gods, looked upon me and
2 CONT #Nabu-na’id (my) only son, the issue of my womb, to the kingship
2 CONT #he called, and the kingship of Sumer and Akkad
2 CONT #from the border of Egypt (on) the upper sea even to the lower sea
2 CONT #all the lands he entrusted hither
2 CONT #to his hands. My two hands I lifted up and to Sin, king of the gods,
2 CONT #reverently with imploration [(I prayed) thus, " Nabu-na’id
2 CONT #(my) son, offspring of my womb, beloved of his mother,]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Col. II.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #thou hast called him to the kingship, thou hast pronounced his name,
2 CONT #at the command of thy great godhead may the great gods
2 CONT #go at his two sides, may they make his enemies to fall,
2 CONT #forget not, (but) make good E-hul-hul and the finishing of its foundation (?)
2 CONT #When in my dream, his two hands had been laid on, Sin, king of the gods,
2 CONT #spoke to me thus, " With thee I will put into the hands of Nabu-na’id, thy son, the return of the gods and the habitation of Harran ;
2 CONT #He shall build E-hul-hul, shall perfect its structure, (and) Harran
2 CONT #more than (it was) before he shall perfect and restore it to its place.
2 CONT #The hand of Sin, Nin-gal, Nusku, and Sadarnunna
2 CONT #I. he shall clasp and cause them to enter E-hul-hul ". The word of Sin,
2 CONT #king of the gods, which he spoke to me I honoured, and I myself saw (it fulfilled);
2 CONT #Nabu-na’id, (my) only son, offspring of my womb, the rites
2 CONT #forgotten of Sin, Nin-gal, Nusku, and
2 CONT #Sadarnunna he perfected, E-hul-hul
2 CONT #anew he built and perfected its structure, Harran more
2 CONT #than before he perfected and restored it to its place ; the hand
2 CONT #of Sin, Nin-gal, Nusku, and Sadarnunna from
2 CONT #Suanna his royal city he clasped, and in the midst of Harran
2 CONT #in E-hul-hul the abode of their hearts’ ease with gladness
2 CONT #and rejoicing he let them dwell. What from former times Sin, king of the gods,
2 CONT #had not done and had not granted to anybody (he did) for the love of me
2 CONT #who had ever worshipped his godhead, laid hold on the hem of his robe-Sin, king of the gods,
2 CONT #uplifted my head and set upon me a good name in the land,
2 CONT #long days, years of heart’s ease he multiplied upon me.
2 CONT #From the time of Assurbanipal, king of Assyria, until the 9th year
2 CONT #of Nabu-na’id king of Babylon, the son, offspring of my womb
2 CONT #104 years of happiness, with the reverence which Sin, king of the gods,
2 CONT #placed in me, he made me flourish, my own self : the sight of my two eyes
2 CONT #is clear, I am excellent in understanding, my hand and both feet are sound,
2 CONT #well-chosen are my words, meat and drink
2 CONT #agree with me, my flesh is goodly, glad is my heart.
2 CONT #My descendants to four generations from me flourishing in themselves
2 CONT #I have seen, I am fulfilled (with) offspring. O Sin, king of the gods, for favour
2 CONT #thou hast looked upon me, thou hast lengthened my days : Nabu-na’id, king of Babylon,
2 CONT #my son, to Sin my lord I have devoted him. So long as he is alive
2 CONT #let him not offend against thee ; the genius of favour, genius of favour which (to be) with me
2 CONT #thou hast appointed and they have caused me to attain offspring, with him (too)
2 CONT #appoint (them), and wickedness and offense against thy great godhead
2 CONT #endure not, (but) let him worship thy great godhead. In the 2I years
2 CONT #of Nabopolassar, king of Babylon, in the 43 years of Nebuchadrezzar,
2 CONT #son of Nabopolassar, and 4 years of Neriglissar, king of Babylon,
2 CONT #(when) they exercised the kingship, for 68 years
2 CONT #with all my heart I reverenced them, I kept watch over them,
2 CONT #Nabu-na’id (my) son, offspring of my womb, before Nebuchadrezzar
2 CONT #son of Nabopolassar and (before) Neriglissar, king of Babylon, I caused him to stand,
2 CONT #daytime and night he kept watch over them
2 CONT #what was pleaSing to them he performed continually,
2 CONT #my name he made (to be) favourite in their sight, (and) like
2 CONT #[a daughter of] their [own] they uplifted my head
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Col. III.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #I nourished (their spirits), and incense offering
2 CONT #rich, of sweet savour,
2 CONT #I appointed for them continually and
2 CONT #laid ever before them.
2 CONT #(Now) in the 9th year of Nabu-na’id,
2 CONT #king of Babylon, the fate
2 CONT #of herself carried her off, and
2 CONT #Nabu-na’id, king of Babylon,
2 CONT #(her) son, issue of her womb, . . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #her corpse entombed, and [robes]
2 CONT #splendid, a bright mantle. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #gold, bright. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #beautiful stones, [precious] stones,
2 CONT #costly stones. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #sweet oil her corpse he [anointed]
2 CONT #they laid it in a secret place. [Oxen and]
2 CONT #sheep (especially) fattened he [slaughtered]
2 CONT #before it. He assembled [the people]
2 CONT #of Babylon and Borsippa, [with the people]
2 CONT #dwelling in far regions, [kings, princes, and]
2 CONT #governors, from [the border]
2 CONT #of Egypt on the Upper Sea
2 CONT #(even) to the Lower Sea he [made to come up],
2 CONT #mourning and
2 CONT #weeping he performed, [dust ?]
2 CONT #they cast upon their heads, for 7 days
2 CONT #and 7 nights with. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #they cut themselves(?), their clothes
2 CONT #were cast down(?). On the seventh day. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #the people(?) of all the land their hair(?)
2 CONT #shaved, and. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #their clothes. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #the . . . . . . . . . . . of their clothes. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #in(?) their places(?). . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #they ? to. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #at meat (?). . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #perfumes refined he amassed (?). . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #sweet oil upon the heads [of the people]
2 CONT #he poured out, their hearts. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #he made glad, he [cheered (?)]
2 CONT #their minds, the road [to their homes]
2 CONT #he did not(?) withhold(?). . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #to their own places they went.
2 CONT #Do thou, whether a king or a prince. . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Remainder too fragmentary for translation until: --)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Fear (the gods), in heaven and earth
2 CONT #pray to them, [neglect] not [the utterance]
2 CONT #of the mouth of Sin and the goddess
2 CONT #. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
2 CONT #- - -. . . . make safe the . . . . . . . . . . . of thy seed
2 CONT #[ever(?)] and for [ever(?)].
2 CONT
