2 CONT Tiglath-Pileser IIFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to: navigation, search Tiglath-Pileser II (from the Hebraic form[1] of Akkadian Tukultī-apil-Ešarra) was King of Assyria from 967 BCE, when he succeeded his father Ashur-
2 CONC resh-ishi II until his death in 935 BCE, when he was succeeded by his son Ashur-dan II. Little is known about his reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] See also Ancient Near East portal Tiglath-Pileser Tiglath-Pileser III [edit] Notes1.^ "Tiglath-pileser", 2Kings 15:29); or "Tilgath-pilneser", 2Chronicles 28:20. [edit] References This article incorporates text from a publi
