1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adasi_%28Assyria%29 '''Adasi'''] was an [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assyria Assyrian] king, the last in a line of 7 kings designated by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_A
2 CONC ssyrian_kings Assyrian King List] as usurpers of the Assyrian throne, who reigned from 1720 - 1701 BC after the ejection of the Amorite ruled [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylonia Babylonians] from Assyria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He is credited''' in the Assyrian King List with stabilising Assyria and freeing it from civil war and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amorites Amorite] influence. The Adaside dynasty of Assyria was named after him. He was succe
2 CONC eded by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bel-bani Bel-bani].
2 CONT
